 "written_from": "company/product/2026-10-28-world-brief.md section 10, R-LEGACY-QV (head-of-product, 2026-10-28) and section 3.2 rules 1 to 6, on origin/product/world-brief-rulings. Nothing else: no M1 code was read, and none exists. The expected states are the ruling applied by hand.",
 "ruling": "A null-qv recall counts, once engineering's writer proof exists (3.2 rule 6), as the question version current when M1 is released, pinned per lesson in the M1 record. (1) It stops counting once that lesson's question changes after M1. (2) It never counts if the question changed after the record's time but before M1.",
 "frozen": "Same terms as m1-histories.json: committed before the M1 maker's first commit under src/; edited after that commit it is void for EXP-012 P1.1. A correction goes in a newer dated file.",
 "how_to_read": {
  "same_as": "m1-histories.json how_to_read, plus the four additions below. All other rules, the vocabulary, the units (ms from t0) and the expect shape are unchanged.",
  "m1_release_at_ms": "The moment M1 is released. Every record in pre_m1 is dated before it. The World's state function is read only from m1_release_at_ms on, so steps start with the m1_release event at that instant.",
  "pre_m1": "What existed before M1: records (reveals, and recalls with source null and qv null), and qv_changes ({lesson, at_ms, qv}: the lesson's question becomes qv at that time). current_qv is each lesson's version at t0, before any qv_change. A history with account rows instead of local records gives them in the m1_release event's account_rows, and no device holds them until a sync step.",
  "at_release": "What engineering's M1 record must show for the history: pinned_qv (each lesson's version current at m1_release_at_ms) and changed_after_record_before_m1 (the lessons with a null-qv recall and a question change after that recall and before M1; empty if none).",
  "m1_release": "The event at the first step. After it, steps use the original vocabulary. A qv_change event after it is a change after M1 (no at_ms: it applies at now_ms)."
 },
 "readings_chosen": [
  "A null-qv recall made after a question change (change at_ms earlier than the record's at_ms) is not blocked: it was made against the changed question. Row legacy-qv-a-change-before-the-record-does-not-block-it. If head-of-product reads 'changed since the record' differently, that row and only that row changes.",
  "Condition 2 is permanent for the record: once it fails at M1 the record never counts again, whatever later happens. Only answers carrying a source and a qv can restore the state.",
  "The proof gate (3.2 rule 6) is checked first and independently: without it nothing counts, changed or not. Row legacy-qv-needs-the-writer-proof.",
  "Not asserted anywhere: whether a counted record is rewritten with its pinned version on sync (these rows never assert a synced record's qv); and a null-qv recall that arrives from an old client after M1 (the ruling speaks of pre-M1 records)."
 ],
